Thank you for sharing the records. Peer support in early psychosis is a promising and growing area. Taken together, the studies you retrieved suggest that peer support workers can improve engagement and hope, that feasibility trials in similar teams have recruited reasonably well, and that peer workers themselves need clear roles and supervision to stay in post. Disengagement in the first year is common, and questionnaire completion falls among younger participants. I would recommend a feasibility study with progression criteria covering recruitment, retention, delivery and questionnaire completion. If it would help, I can set this out as a structured appraisal with ratings for each study and a list of claims linked to the evidence.